## Hello: the smallest library, one greeting. A library is an ordinary
## file whose exported names start with l:; libraries of your own live
## in userlibs/, on the search path. demos/hello-library.xtl imports it
## ("hi:" u_se< "Hello"), and docs/literate/hello.org walks through
## both. The name in the string is the logo: typed X_ e:T a:L, drawn,
## spaces removed (a string may hold any Unicode).

## The greeting, as text (niladic: call it with @).
## >> "hi:" u_se< "Hello"
## >> hi:h_ello @
## hello X̲ᵉTᵃL
l:h_ello := { @ -> "hello X̲ᵉTᵃL" }        # niladic: call it with @
